  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You’re given an array AAA containing NNN integers. Your task is to make Ai≥0A_i \\geq 0Ai​≥0 for all 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.\n\nTo achieve that, you can perform the following operation:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i&lt;N1 \\le i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N) and any integer XXX (XXX can be negative);\nSubtract XXX from AiA_iAi​ and add XXX to Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​.\n\nThat is, set Ai:=Ai−XA_i:= A_i - XAi​:=Ai​−X and Ai+1:=Ai+1+XA_{i+1} := A_{i+1} + XAi+1​:=Ai+1​+X.\nFind the **minimum** number of operations necessary to make Ai≥0A_i \\geq 0Ai​≥0 for all iii.\n\nIf it's impossible to achieve this, output −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, denoting the length of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the minimum number of operations needed to make Ai≥0A_i \\geq 0Ai​≥0 for all 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.\n\nIf it's not possible to achieve this no matter what, output −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 -2\n3\n-3 2 1\n6\n-2 1 1 1 1 -2",
        "output": "-1\n2\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The only possible operation is to add some XXX to A1A_1A1​ and subtract the same XXX from A2A_2A2​.\nWith just this, it's not possible to have both A1≥0A_1\\geq 0A1​≥0 and A2≥0A_2\\geq 0A2​≥0 simultaneously.\nTest case 222: One way of using two operations is as follows:\n\nInitially, A=[−3,2,1]A = [-3, 2, 1]A=[−3,2,1].\nChoose i=2i=2i=2 and X=−1X=-1X=−1. After this operation, A=[−3,3,0]A=[-3,3,0]A=[−3,3,0].\nChoose i=1i=1i=1 and X=−3X=-3X=−3. After this operation, A=[0,0,0]A=[0,0,0]A=[0,0,0] and we're done.\n\nIt can be shown that using only one operation is not enough."
      }
    ]
